From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 22:16:54 +0200
Subject: mtd: rawnand: lantiq-xrx500: give the byte handshake its own wait

xrx500_nand_waitrdy() answers two different questions with one predicate.
EBU_WAIT_WR_C says the EBU has finished the bus cycle for the byte just
strobed; EBU_WAIT_RDBY is R/B#, and says the chip has finished the
operation it was given. The byte paths want the first, the WAITRDY
instruction wants the second, and the "or" between them lets either
caller conclude on the other's flag.

Split the byte handshake out into xrx500_nand_wait_latch() with its own
budget, so that the chip-ready wait can later be narrowed without taking
the byte paths with it. No functional change: both helpers still test
the same pair of bits, in the same order, with the same timeouts.

While the byte paths are being touched, propagate their errors. The
timeout was discarded at every level -- writeb() and readb() returned
void, the buf loops could not report, and exec_op() had no way to learn
that a strobe had gone unanswered -- so a hung EBU cycle was reported to
the NAND core as a completed operation. The address loop becomes
xrx500_nand_write_addrs() rather than growing an error break inside the
switch, which keeps the instruction dispatch one statement per case.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

